<title>THAILAND: Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Jan 30.</title>
<headline>Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Jan 30.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry and independent surveyors detailed rice loading at Thai ports as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel		Date of Arrival   Quantity     Destination</p>
<p>Sengcheng	   07/01/97		5,000	  Singapore</p>
<p>Deltgst	     08/01/97		4,000	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Sangthai Glory    08/01/97		5,000	  Hong Kong</p>
<p>Sangthai Winner   09/01/97		3,000	  Hong Kong</p>
<p>Sangthai Ceramic  09/01/97		1,500	  Hong Kong</p>
<p>Ekraj Dakal	 09/01/97		5,000	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Sangthai Heaven   10/01/97		3,000	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Dibenawin	   10/01/97		6,900	  Malaysia</p>
<p>Lennon		10/01/97		5,000	  Japan</p>
<p>Seac Kraland	10/01/97		3,000	  Japan</p>
<p>Anlujiang	   10/01/97	     13,000	  Iran</p>
<p>Sejing		10/01/97		4,800	  China</p>
<p>Bangkhon Tee	16/01/97		5,000	  Bunai</p>
<p>Sangthai Scenic   16/01/97		2,000	  Hong Kong</p>
<p>Ekraj Seacon	16/01/97		5,000	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Siam Sero	   17/01/97		5,500	  Japan</p>
<p>Panya Sakorn	17/01/97		5,800	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Budiain	     17/01/97		3,500	  Indonesia</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
